## Original Content
<p>Today I’m excited to share that we are expanding our university content catalog with new certificates and Specializations that are designed to help learners develop the human and technical skills that matter most in an AI-powered future. Findings from more than 92,000 employers included in the QS World Future Skills Index 2027 show persistent gaps [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://blog.coursera.org/new-university-programs-help-learners-build-skills-for-the-ai-era/">New university programs help learners build human and technical skills for the AI era</a> appeared first on <a href="https://blog.coursera.org">Coursera Blog</a>.</p>

## Summary
Coursera is expanding its university offerings with new certificates and Specializations aimed at helping learners build human and technical skills for an AI-powered future. These programs are informed by employer insights from the QS World Future Skills Index 2027, which reveals persistent skill gaps in the workforce.

## Key Points
- New certificates and Specializations are being added to the university content catalog.
- The programs focus on developing both human and technical skills for the AI era.
- Insights are derived from over 92,000 employers via the QS World Future Skills Index 2027.
- Persistent skill gaps have been identified by employers in the context of AI and future work.


